{"name":"Sommelier","hex":"#5d3736","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sommelier","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The member of staff at a restaurant who keeps the wine cellar and advises the guests on a choice of wines; a wine steward / stewardess, a wine waiter / waitress / server."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act as a sommelier."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sommelier"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sommelier","blocks":[{"text":"A sommelier, chef de vin or wine steward, is a trained and knowledgeable wine professional, normally working in fine restaurants, who specializes in all aspects of wine service as well as wine and food pairing. The role of the sommelier in fine dining today is much more specialized and informed than that of a wine waiter. Sommeliers Australia states that the role is strategically on par with that of the chef de cuisine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Sommelier_F.I.S.A.R..jpg/330px-Sommelier_F.I.S.A.R..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sommelier","wikidata":"Q191493"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Corkscrew_-_sommelier_knife.jpg/500px-Corkscrew_-_sommelier_knife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Corkscrew_-_sommelier_knife.jpg/1280px-Corkscrew_-_sommelier_knife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Corkscrew_-_sommelier_knife.jpg/500px-Corkscrew_-_sommelier_knife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The sommelier knife is an important tool of the sommelier.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorkscrew_-_sommelier_knife.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Tastevin.jpg/500px-Tastevin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Tastevin.jpg/1280px-Tastevin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Tastevin.jpg/500px-Tastevin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The tastevin vessel used by sommeliers in the past is still a symbol today.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATastevin.jpg"}],"sounds":{"sommelier":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/En-au-sommelier.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a9/En-au-sommelier.ogg/En-au-sommelier.ogg.mp3"}]}}}